'''Manifest Dancing Dervishes''' is a [[spell]] granted by {{il|The Dancing Dervish}}. This spell summons two dancing dervish [[minion]]s, while disabling the character's weapon. The character has [[Onslaught]] while the dancing dervishes remain alive.

==Skill functions and interactions==
Manifest Dancing Dervishes summons two dancing dervish minions. It is [[trigger]]ed when the character reaches the first [[Rampage]] tier of 15 consecutive kills. While the dancing dervishes remain alive, the character has [[Onslaught]] and their weapon is disabled.

Manifest Dancing Dervishes cannot be supported by support gems that create other minions, such as {{il|Summon Phantasm Support}}. Manifest Dancing Dervishes cannot be supported by {{il|Enhance}}, {{il|Enlighten}} or {{il|Empower}}, as these only support skill gems.

The dancing dervishes use {{sl|id=DancingDervishCycloneChannelled}}, a [[channelling]] melee attack skill. It is functionally similar to the {{il|Cyclone}} skill gem version. Support gems that can support Manifest Dancing Dervishes also apply to the dancing dervish minions and their Cyclone skill.

The dancing dervishes do not have a timed [[duration]]. Instead, they remain alive as long as the player can keep up their character's [[Rampage]] kill streak. As they are minions, the dancing dervishes' kills do count toward Rampage. Additionally, each time a dancing dervish [[hit]]s a rare or unique monster, there is a 25% chance to add 1 to the character's Rampage kill counter.

Dancing dervishes are considered to be manifested minions, which allows them to be used while the character is equipped with {{il|Chains of Command}}. Dancing dervishes are ''not'' considered to be [[Animate Weapon|animated weapons]].

{{Alternate skill effect list|skill=Cyclone}}

Alternate skill effects for {{il|Cyclone}} can be applied to Manifest Dancing Dervishes.

